{{2026 UCI Road World Championships}}

The '''[[UCI Road World Championships&nbsp;– Men's under-23 road race|Men's under-23 road race]]''' of the [[2026 UCI Road World Championships]] was a cycling event that took place on 25 September 2026 in [[Montreal]], [[Canada]]. It was the 5th edition of the championship, for which [[Lorenzo Finn]] of [[Italy]] was the defending champion, having won in [[2025 UCI Road World Championships&nbsp;– Men's under-23 road race|2025]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.montreal2026.org/en/challenge/mens-u23-road-race/|title=Men's Under-23 Road Race|accessdate=25 September 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.cyclingnews.com/pro-cycling/racing/uci-road-world-championships-ashlin-barry-powers-to-under-23-mens-title-with-30-kilometre-solo-attack/|title=UCI Road World Championships: Ashlin Barry powers to under-23 men's title with 30-kilometre solo attack
|publisher=CyclingNews|first1=Kirsten|last1=Frattini|first2=Laura|last2=Weislo|date=25 September 2026|accessdate=25 September 2026}}</ref>

